# Create Model

Model owns state, bindings, and interaction logic. It is the brain of a feature.

## Use when

A feature needs state, bindings, selection, validation state, or UI orchestration.

## Put in Model

- JavaFX properties
- computed bindings
- selection, form, and filter state
- validation flags
- command or service triggering

## Keep out

- raw node construction
- large backend logic
- low-level controller event boilerplate

## Key API

- extend `DefaultModel<M, V>`, or `DefaultFXMLModel<M>` when the view is FXML.
- link sibling models with the `@Link` annotation.
- set up bindings in `bind()`.
- react to messages with `@OnWave(SomeWaves.WT)`; emit with `sendWave(...)`.
- run actions with `callCommand(SomeCommand.class, WBuilder.waveData(ITEM, value))`.

Template: `templates/ModelTemplate.java.txt`.
